<article class="env-lemma" id="06EB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06EB">Lemma <span data-tag="06EB">29.16.6</span>.</a> Let $f : T \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $f$ is locally of finite type and surjective, then $f(T_{\text{ft-pts}}) = S_{\text{ft-pts}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have $f(T_{\text{ft-pts}}) \subset S_{\text{ft-pts}}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/02J3" data-tag="02J3">29.16.5</a>. Let $s \in S$ be a finite type point. As $f$ is surjective the scheme $T_ s = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\kappa (s)) \times _ S T$ is nonempty, therefore has a finite type point $t \in T_ s$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/02J2" data-tag="02J2">29.16.4</a>. Now $T_ s \to T$ is a morphism of finite type as a base change of $s \to S$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/01T4" data-tag="01T4">29.15.4</a>). Hence the image of $t$ in $T$ is a finite type point by Lemma <a href="/tag/02J3" data-tag="02J3">29.16.5</a> which maps to $s$ by construction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>